ces at the Center, Both Handed Back", "summary": "The 20k, playing Black, won by 74 points when both players passed. GPT-6.1 Sol kept the game close early, with the lead at -0.4 after move 2 and -0.3 after move 4. After move 12, though, the lead stayed in Black's favour for the rest of the game. Sol averaged 10.1 points lost per move with 15 blunders, against 7.4 and 9 for the 20k. Swings of 25 points or more at moves 29 to 32 and again at 36, 37 and 40 to 43 turned a lead into a rout.", "moments": [{"turn": 18, "text": "White crawled along the edge with B3, losing 15.8 points and raising Black's lead from +21.7 to +37.5. The engine preferred E6. A3 and A4 followed, losing 18.1 and 17.8, and the edge crawl left the centre unattended."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "The 20k's E5 was the worst move of the game, losing 33.9 points and cutting Black's lead from +42.6 to +8.8. The engine's choice was H4. For one moment the game was nearly open again."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol answered with G3, which lost 28.7 points, and Black's lead jumped from +8.8 back to +37.5. The engine wanted G5. This was Sol's worst move, and it gave the chance back immediately."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "C8 lost 27.6 points and took Black's lead from +43.8 to +71.4, where D2 was the engine's pick. The 20k's E8 reply lost 28.6, but Black was so far ahead that the lead only came back to +42.7."}, {"turn": 52, "text": "Late in the game, H1 lost 25.8 points and lifted the lead from +46.4 to +72.2. The engine's choice was F1, which Black then took. After that the lead stayed at +72.2 through the passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either played a single move the player named via mcp__go__play, logged raw responses, or ran the verification file, which only replays recorded moves and flood-fills boards for groups, liberties and area counts. Nothing looped over empty points to rank moves or played continuations forward to choose a move; the failed AGE